executable: no shell/exec tool and no HEAD-write tool in this runtime` plus a copy-paste hand-over block (with mandatory `-- pathspec`) \\u2014 nothing committed, escalation to a human operator.\",\n  \"message_count\": 31,\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Raised by PM in shift 5 (2026-11-18T16:33Z) from a measurement of the working tree. This replaces the vague step \\\"commit the efforts work\\\" in milestone M1, which was never scoped.\\n\\nWHY: `git status` vs HEAD is 65 changed files in `src/` + `tests/`, +2219/-221. It mixes at least four unrelated in-flight features (browsers/volume mappings, chat find bar, voice, the recurrence UI in TaskSettings.vue) with the efforts increment. Committing that as one commit destroys the increment's only real property: that it can be deployed, demoed and reverted on its own. It also hides the efforts work from review inside 2200 lines nobody will read.\\n\\nEXACT PATHS TO COMMIT (the whole efforts increment):\\n1. `src/api/modules/efforts.js`                 (+8/-3)   behaviour change\\n2. `src/components/global_settings/EffortsSettings.vue` (+8/-1)  remove() fix \\u2014 card fcf65219\\n3. `tests/effortsApi.test.mjs`                  (A, +139) 9 cases \\u2014 card d4e3a041\\n4. `package.json` \\u2014 ONLY the `\\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test tests/\\\"` hunk (+1 line at :14).\\n\\nDELIBERATELY OUT OF THIS COMMIT:\\n- `src/components/kanban/TaskSettings.vue` (+123/-0) = the RECURRENCE feature, a different increment. Do not commit it here.\\n- `package.json` hunk 2: `vue3-virtual-scroller ^0.2.3 -> ^2.0.3`, an unowned MAJOR dependency bump. Stage the test-script hunk only (`git add -p package.json`) and leave the bump dirty.\\n- every browsers/ chat/ voice/ volumeMappings file, and the untracked `tests/voice*.test.mjs` suites.\\n\\nORDER (hard): 91411767 (node runtime) -> 675c4695 (delete the 3 HTML-comment lines, else the CISO gate blocks on scope=all) -> a0f362ed (9 ok lines posted) -> this commit. Do not commit before the 9 `ok -` lines exist: an unverified behaviour change in a commit is the exact thing this increment exists to prevent.\\n\\nACCEPTANCE:\\n- `git show --stat HEAD` lists exa",
          "output": "### Task `efforts increment: commit by explicit pathspec (3 files + 1 hunk) \u2014 recurrence, browsers, voice and the vue3-virtual-scroller major bump stay out`\n- ID: `0bc8b144-7506-415d-ac07-469043b98b04`\n- Status: `onhold` | Mode: `chat`\n- Board: `IT team` | Column: `Working`\n- Sprints: none\n- Priority: `high` | Progress: 60% | Due: `2026-11-19` | Wake: `2026-11-20T13:00:00+00:00`\n- Assignees: software_developer\n- Updated: 2026-11-19T14:34:48.659505\n- Description: 1. **Task:** land the efforts increment as ONE commit of exactly 3 client paths (`efforts.js`, `EffortsSettings.vue`, `tests/effortsApi.test.mjs`), leaving the `package.json` vue3-virtual-scroller **downgrade** dirty.\n2. **Gate change:** PM withdrew the \"9 `ok -` lines first\" precondition \u2014 node/npm do not exist in the runtime (`91411767`), so the commit proceeds without executed tests as an accepted residual risk.\n3. **Measured each shift, unchanged:** HEAD stays `dba24f4`, the 3 paths still dirty (+8/\u22123, +8/\u22121, +3/\u22125 = +19/\u22129), `package.json` still +1/\u22121, index polluted with ~102 `.codx/` entries so only a pathspec commit is safe.\n4. **Blocker:** the runtime has **no shell/exec tool**, so `git add`/`git commit` cannot be run; per the card I attempted no workaround, used no branch-commit or file-write substitute.\n5. **Outcome:** posted `commit not executable: no shell/exec tool and no HEAD-write tool in this runtime` plus a copy-paste hand-over block (with mandatory `-- pathspec`) \u2014 nothing committed, escalation to a human operator.\n\n**Conversation**\n> Last 8 of 31 visible message(s)\n- **assistant**: Ping from the verification card `f48294e8` (shift 6, turn 2, ~14:15Z): **still no commit.** HEAD `dba24f4bf27c` unchanged; the 3 paths remain dirty `M` (+8/\u22123, +8/\u22121, +3/\u22125).  One correction to *my own* recipe (comment 10), measured with `project_changes(base=\"HEAD~1\")`: `tests/effortsApi.test.mjs` ...\n- **assistant