            "comment": "**Pre-loaded facts for the 16:00Z decision \u2014 the question has moved since this card was written.**\n\nThe scenario this card was built for (\"commit the increment with no executed tests\") no longer applies: **there is nothing left to commit.** The three efforts paths and `package.json` are clean vs HEAD and carry the fixed content \u2014 `efforts.js` returns the envelope, `EffortsSettings.vue` `remove()` throws on `status_code` (:376), `tests/effortsApi.test.mjs` has its 9 cases (139 lines), `package.json` has `\"test\": \"node --test tests/\"` and `^0.2.3`. So the increment is *already shipped in a commit*; the open question is retroactive.\n\nRestated decision: **do we accept the efforts delete fix as M1 content while its 9 tests have never been executed?** Constraints, unchanged: no node/npm in this runtime (91411767), so the suite cannot run here at all; the fix is 5 lines of guard code in a screen that fails visibly (red banner), not silently.\n\nMy recommendation, and the only option I can defend to management alone: **B for M1, A as the definition of done before the customer flag flip.**\n- **B (recommended):** demo M1 on the delete behaviour \u2014 built-in effort \u2192 red banner, throwaway effort \u2192 disappears (script already on card 2cd6e1f6). Acceptance is by observed behaviour, and the test file travels as a spare that someone runs in a node-capable environment (card a0f362ed). Risk accepted and *written down*.\n- **A:** block M1 until the 9 tests run somewhere with node. Cost: unknown external lead time, no date I can commit to, and M1 loses the 11-23 demo.\n- **C:** revert the delete fix and demo only list/edit. Cleanest verification story, reopens card fcf65219 and makes the delete button lie again \u2014 a worse defect than an unrun test.\n\nSo: B now, and the decision that actually needs management is a *deadline* \u2014 by when must a node-capable environment exist, or the 9 tests stop being \"temporarily unrun\" and become \"never written\". My proposal: 2026-11-27, tied to 91411767."
